","name":"swift/baseline/expected-extracted-files","shortDescription":{"text":"Expected extracted files"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Files appearing in the source archive that are expected to be extracted."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true},"properties":{"tags":["expected-extracted-files","telemetry"]}},{"id":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","name":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","shortDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"fullDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}},{"id":"cli/platform","name":"cli/platform","shortDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}}],"rules":[{"id":"py/augur/tensorflow/pass2-command-injection","name":"py/augur/tensorflow/pass2-command-injection","shortDescription":{"text":"TensorFlow Pass 2: Command/Argument Injection (CWE-78)"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Tracks untrusted input into command execution sinks in the TensorFlow Python layer. Sources are the reviewed pass-2 tp labels: the tfdbg gRPC debug-server receive boundary (SendEvents / SendTracebacks / SendSourceFiles request parameters and the on_value_event / on_graph_def / on_core_metadata_event stream-handler callbacks of the unauthenticated [::]:port listener), sys.argv / parse_args / parse_known_args / input() CLI boundaries in runtime library entry points, and urlopen network responses. Sinks are the reviewed subprocess execution sites: the run_shell_cmd Popen(shell=True) string command and the argv-list Popen / check_output / check_call / call / run commands with environment- or parameter-influenced operands (configure.py PYTHON_BIN_PATH, flatc / git / grep / objdump / gcloud tooling). Sanitizer: shlex.quote / _shlex_quote (saved_model_aot_compile.py). Additional taint steps: the three tfdbg stream_handler.on_* dispatch hops. Sources, sinks, sanitizers and summaries are Phase 1 reviewed labels from run tensorflow-iris-pass2-labeling-20261016; a finding is a review candidate, not a confirmed vulnerability - the reviewed exec sites have static, internally derived or list-form operands, so no complete source-to-sink path is expected in this snapshot."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-078","external/cwe/cwe-077","external/cwe/cwe-088"],"description":"Tracks untrusted input into command execution sinks in the TensorFlow\n   Python layer. Sources are the reviewed pass-2 tp labels: the tfdbg gRPC\n   debug-server receive boundary (SendEvents / SendTracebacks /\n   SendSourceFiles request parameters and the on_value_event / on_graph_def\n   / on_core_metadata_event stream-handler callbacks of the unauthenticated\n   [::]:port listener), sys.argv / parse_args / parse_known_args / input()\n   CLI boundaries in runtime library entry points, and urlopen network\n   responses. Sinks are the reviewed subprocess execution sites: the\n   run_shell_cmd Popen(shell=True) string command and the argv-list\n   Popen / check_output / check_call / call / run commands with\n   environment- or parameter-influenced operands (configure.py\n   PYTHON_BIN_PATH, flatc / git / grep / objdump / gcloud tooling).\n   Sanitizer: shlex.quote / _shlex_quote (saved_model_aot_compile.py).\n   Additional taint steps: the three tfdbg stream_handler.on_* dispatch\n   hops. Sources, sinks, sanitizers and summaries are Phase 1 reviewed\n   labels from run tensorflow-iris-pass2-labeling-20261016; a finding is a review candidate, not a confirmed\n   vulnerability - the reviewed exec sites have static, internally\n   derived or list-form operands, so no complete source-to-sink path is\n   expected in this snapshot.","id":"py/augur/tensorflow/pass2-command-injection","kind":"path-problem","name":"TensorFlow Pass 2: Command/Argument Injection (CWE-78)","precision":"low","problem.severity":"error"}}]},"extensions":[{"name":"iris/tensorflow-cwe78","semanticVersion":"0.0.1","l